<title>UK: Canada's Goodale defends CWB role in grain trade.</title>
<headline>Canada's Goodale defends CWB role in grain trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian minister Ralph Goodale on Thursday defended the Canadian Wheat Board against its international detractors.</p>
<p>Goodale, the minister who has responsibility for the CWB, told the International Grains Council's conference in London that the workings of the board system were not incompatible with the aim of liberalising world trade.</p>
<p>&quot;Just because one form of marketing system is different from another doesn't mean they cannot operate under the same disciplines,&quot; Goodale said.</p>
<p>For over 50 years the CWB, with what Goodale described as a &quot;single desk marketing system,&quot; had been a reliable supplier to international grains markets, he said.</p>
</text>
